 {:db/id "q-216463" :question/id #uuid "6336cc3e-143c-5d52-83b4-52b2733f351b" :question/math-academy-id "q-216463" :question/problem "$\\,$ $P(x):{x}^{2}>x$\n\nGiven the predicate above, which of the following expresses the statement $∀x\\in (1,\\infty ),\\,P(x)?$" :question/worked-solution "The universal quantifier \"$∀$\" means \"for all.\" So, the statement \n$∀x\\in (1,\\infty ),\\,P(x)$ \nreads as follows:\n\n$\\,$ **For all** $x\\in (1,\\infty ),$ ${x}^{2}>x.$\n\n**Note:** This statement is true." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-216463/ma-source-field/d0d2cc2c0c6346f498e3bbafb5ea20945e5dc6c7d628e16956afb317faaac413"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
