 {:db/id "q-2194" :question/id #uuid "6e0472f6-3d3e-5a0e-bbc2-09db07e6e756" :question/math-academy-id "q-2194" :question/problem "Calculate the integral $\\int \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's set $u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x.$ Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=\\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\sqrt{2}\\int \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{x} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\cdot \\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|+C \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{ln}⁡x|+C\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-2194/ma-source-field/88a5daef7dbad81c64e9c97a558e753d9d2c52beab47f6eace95523fc5dd5eb5"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
