 {:db/id [:question/id #uuid "fcb31a9b-9679-5d24-8bf7-7929bd2e8a6c"] :question/problem "Which of the following equations has no solutions for $0\\le x<2\\pi ?$\n\nI. $\\operatorname{sec}⁡x=1$\nII. $\\operatorname{sec}⁡x=2$\nIII. $\\operatorname{sec}⁡x=\\frac{1}{2}$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the range of $\\operatorname{sec}⁡x$ for $0\\le x<2\\pi $ is given by\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\in (-\\infty ,-1]\\cup [1,\\infty ).\n$$\n\nSo, the equation $\\operatorname{sec}⁡x=k$ has no solutions for $k\\in (-1,1).$ \n\nTherefore, of the given equations, only equation III has no solutions." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-29163/ma-source-field/bbb4f56cdee6e01ad4c052af3078448aabb72e3bb1148d0d58dcc606781e2311"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
