 {:db/id "q-29477" :question/id #uuid "2c11092b-9e53-51e1-b299-c5287bf677e1" :question/math-academy-id "q-29477" :question/problem "Which of the following equations has no solutions for $0\\le x<2\\pi ?$\n\nI. $\\operatorname{csc}⁡x=\\frac{1}{3}$\nII. $\\operatorname{csc}⁡x=3$\nIII. $\\operatorname{csc}⁡x=1$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the range of $\\operatorname{csc}⁡x$ for $0\\le x<2\\pi $ is given by\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\in (-\\infty ,-1]\\cup [1,\\infty ).\n$$\n\nSo, the equation $\\operatorname{csc}⁡x=k$ has no solutions for $k\\in (-1,1).$ \n\nTherefore, of the given equations, only equation I has no solutions." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-29477/ma-source-field/44d4bbf840cf85972702cbf0ab32709f8269554916508e09e28c375abd122a03"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
