 {:db/id "q-31919" :question/id #uuid "561c404c-366e-5e58-b3aa-1094d48ff6e7" :question/math-academy-id "q-31919" :question/problem "Which of the following completes the statement so that it is true:\n\n*If $det(A)\\ne 0,$ where $A$ is a $2\\times 2$-matrix, then $A$ is $\\text{__________}$ .*\n\nI. invertible\nII. **not ** invertible\nIII. singular" :question/worked-solution "Recall that given $A=[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{11} & {a}_{12} \\\\ {a}_{21} & {a}_{22}\\end{aligned}]$, then according to the invertible matrix theorem the following statements are equivalent:    \n\n- $A$ is invertible.\n\n- The system $Ax=b$ has exactly one solution for any $2\\times 1$ column vector $b.$\n\n- The system $Ax=0$ has the unique zero solution.\n\n- The lines ${a}_{11}x+{a}_{12}y={b}_{1}$ and ${a}_{21}x+{a}_{22}y={b}_{2}$ intersect at exactly one point.\n\n- $det(A)\\ne 0.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's now check our statements.  \n\nNow, since the fifth part of the invertible matrix theorem is true ($det(A)\\ne 0$), all the other parts of the theorem are true too. Therefore, according to the theorem, only option I gives a true statement:\n\n- *If $det(A)\\ne 0$ , then $A$ is invertible.* $\\,✓$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-31919/ma-source-field/44d4bbf840cf85972702cbf0ab32709f8269554916508e09e28c375abd122a03"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
 {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "64b2036f-da0f-59de-8a39-6b33e6cbdd04"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-31919"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}
 {:db/id "q-31945/ma-source-field/64163c4a08db63d1df8a309d5e176b5be5672569913c511407a3c5d8ea8c511c/68aa1ad1169b72612f62ce110c0f885220f59dd1474b509cf7a1beedbc0c1e22" :answer/id #uuid "428db092-3f21-5636-9fa7-75f2fd6123d6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1},\\,{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+(-3){R}_{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]}
 {:db/id "q-31945/ma-source-field/64163c4a08db63d1df8a309d5e176b5be5672569913c511407a3c5d8ea8c511c/4afe1492125f638f67b645998946aec3135dbd4b97cd2f89feb7363d8fbd97ab" :answer/id #uuid "b42745fe-be44-51aa-b6af-8f31a15a57a1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1},\\,{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+\\frac{3}{4}{R}_{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]}
