 {:db/id "q-32373" :question/id #uuid "95526ab5-adbc-57eb-9fe3-cf21f5b51d6d" :question/math-academy-id "q-32373" :question/problem "Which of the following vector-valued functions are continuous at $t=0?$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t) & =⟨{t}^{2},\\,7t+6,\\,3-{t}^{3}⟩ \\\\ g(t) & =⟨1,\\,{t}^{2/3},\\,t⟩ \\\\ h(t) & =⟨{t}^{2},\\,\\sqrt[3]{t},\\,2t+3⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "A vector-valued function is continuous at a point if and only if each of its components is continuous at that point. \n\nLet's consider the functions one-by-one. \n\n- The function $f(t)$ is continuous at $t=0$ because each of its components ${t}^{2}$, $7t+6$ and $3-{t}^{3}$are continuous at $t=0.$\n\n- The function $g(t)$ is continuous at $t=0$ because each of its components $1$,  ${t}^{2/3}$ and $t$  are continuous at $t=0.$\n\n- The function $h(t)$ is continuous at $t=0$ because each of its components ${t}^{2}$, $\\sqrt[3]{t}$ and $2t+3$ are continuous at $t=0.$\n\nTherefore, the answer is:\n\n$\\,$ All the functions are continuous at $t=0$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-32373/ma-source-field/1325d5ce26575cf24baa645e22d412210f01acfeb390bee45cd6f84c963e66ce"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
