 {:db/id "q-324453/ma-source-field/7762cd3e705137a07c5be0495f6abc572279104e946e1d5306772dc5da0fe394" :answer-field/id #uuid "f95e5646-83c9-5ea4-84fa-6be151721bec" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-324453/ma-source-field/7762cd3e705137a07c5be0495f6abc572279104e946e1d5306772dc5da0fe394/81f3613eeddff7c649cf7bff7c825fcefd1e5ef6f9eb2c0a830ab06c51d02ca5" "q-324453/ma-source-field/7762cd3e705137a07c5be0495f6abc572279104e946e1d5306772dc5da0fe394/84c6c5a8ad3bd889927e0990cafba18266f7b85c030d55a5d5dbf46c2bd19461" "q-324453/ma-source-field/7762cd3e705137a07c5be0495f6abc572279104e946e1d5306772dc5da0fe394/74bb06cfc8e1113aa7e9be189036ae37b3a9ba0ba3d0b2503988fd7520b258e0" "q-324453/ma-source-field/7762cd3e705137a07c5be0495f6abc572279104e946e1d5306772dc5da0fe394/4765682070e348c2e5d1d7ac0fe123ce639ac7eda4d5dbd4bc9cae3d8202007b" "q-324453/ma-source-field/7762cd3e705137a07c5be0495f6abc572279104e946e1d5306772dc5da0fe394/3f3772de5db8c8b129a68c1a194ade1b6e5fb046bcccc4069b278f5a85a46ea0"] :answer-field/correct "q-324453/ma-source-field/7762cd3e705137a07c5be0495f6abc572279104e946e1d5306772dc5da0fe394/81f3613eeddff7c649cf7bff7c825fcefd1e5ef6f9eb2c0a830ab06c51d02ca5" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]}
 {:db/id [:question/id #uuid "1b78e718-c7bd-590c-b65a-fabb1ffe4981"] :question/problem "Find the general solution to the system of differential equations \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)={x}_{1}(t)+3{x}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)={x}_{1}(t)-{x}_{2}(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Hint: The eigenvalues of the system's matrix are ${\\lambda }_{1}=-2$ and ${\\lambda }_{2}=2.$*" :question/worked-solution "We need to find the eigenvalues and the eigenvectors of the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}].$\n\n- We are given that the eigenvalues are \n\n$$\n{\\lambda }_{1}=-2\\,\\text{and}\\,{\\lambda }_{2}=2.\n$$\n\n- Let's go through the process of finding the eigenvectors.\n\n- For ${\\lambda }_{1}=-2,$ we get \n\n$$\nA-{\\lambda }_{1}I=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSo, we get an eigenvector \n${v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$\n\n- For ${\\lambda }_{2}=2,$ we get \n\n$$\nA-{\\lambda }_{2}I=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -3\\end{aligned}]∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSo, we get an eigenvector \n${v}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$\n\nNow, we write down the general solution to the given linear system of differential equations: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={c}_{1}{v}_{1}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{1}t}+{c}_{2}{v}_{2}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{2}t} \\\\  & ={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-2t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-324453/ma-source-field/7762cd3e705137a07c5be0495f6abc572279104e946e1d5306772dc5da0fe394"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
