 {:db/id "q-327989" :question/id #uuid "94d96b96-98bb-5063-b4f0-15839c9585ed" :question/math-academy-id "q-327989" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the system of differential equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=3{x}_{1}(t)-{x}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=4{x}_{1}(t)-2{x}_{2}(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Hint: The eigenvalues of the system's matrix are ${\\lambda }_{1}=-1$ and ${\\lambda }_{2}=2.$*" :question/worked-solution "We need to find the eigenvalues and the eigenvectors of the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ 4 & -2\\end{aligned}].$\n\n- We are given that the eigenvalues are \n\n$$\n{\\lambda }_{1}=-1\\,\\text{and}\\,{\\lambda }_{2}=2.\n$$\n\n- Let's go through the process of finding the eigenvectors.\n\n- For ${\\lambda }_{1}=-1,$ we get \n\n$$\nA-{\\lambda }_{1}I=[\\begin{aligned}4 & -1 \\\\ 4 & -1\\end{aligned}]∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -\\frac{1}{4} \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSo, we get an eigenvector \n${v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].$\n\n- For ${\\lambda }_{2}=2,$ we get \n\n$$\nA-{\\lambda }_{2}I=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 4 & -4\\end{aligned}]∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSo, we get an eigenvector \n${v}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$\n\nNow, we write down the general solution to the given linear system of differential equations: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={c}_{1}{v}_{1}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{1}t}+{c}_{2}{v}_{2}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{2}t} \\\\  & ={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-327989/ma-source-field/9755e94cb60960c5e5d363a17e7d7e5e4004af0c2098f13af8db9b97fa1d6a21"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
