 {:db/id "q-33203/ma-source-field/87c43102284dcfeb2638e146ab0d291e49c36333aab1eaa13bc29a1ec11c418e" :answer-field/id #uuid "1ba93ced-d091-5536-afc3-ce47413fdf3f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-33203/ma-source-field/87c43102284dcfeb2638e146ab0d291e49c36333aab1eaa13bc29a1ec11c418e/8eabc610e0beee450932b0688163559b7cbbdd737fec8f9b43c20e9bab177342" "q-33203/ma-source-field/87c43102284dcfeb2638e146ab0d291e49c36333aab1eaa13bc29a1ec11c418e/6672afb35ecc70684c19fda02ae01aa7d48616466dfec3ab6330d3de06cb317b" "q-33203/ma-source-field/87c43102284dcfeb2638e146ab0d291e49c36333aab1eaa13bc29a1ec11c418e/cc8aa555652706aa52382a8e8bc0fae6dd481e2ea644bcef054ef9e568d3b29d" "q-33203/ma-source-field/87c43102284dcfeb2638e146ab0d291e49c36333aab1eaa13bc29a1ec11c418e/21a1f256f143d04819735701c0c15f3f15f013fbbe7efc023437d2654d4e7d28" "q-33203/ma-source-field/87c43102284dcfeb2638e146ab0d291e49c36333aab1eaa13bc29a1ec11c418e/c8041c0b45c7624d574ce5092ae47ec9f4b5f3ba950a413ae68bb2ab9ecc7368"] :answer-field/correct "q-33203/ma-source-field/87c43102284dcfeb2638e146ab0d291e49c36333aab1eaa13bc29a1ec11c418e/cc8aa555652706aa52382a8e8bc0fae6dd481e2ea644bcef054ef9e568d3b29d" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]}
 {:db/id [:question/id #uuid "49e4fa98-401d-5c2d-a49c-1997a8550033"] :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:r=⟨-5,0,1⟩+t⟨-3,1,0⟩,\\,Π:-3x+y-2z+27=0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by writing the equation of the line as\n\n$$\nr=⟨-5-3t,t,1⟩.\n$$\n\nLet's also write the equation of the plane in the dot product form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3x+y-2z+27 & =0 \\\\ -3x+y-2z & =-27 \\\\ ⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨-3,1,-2⟩ & =-27 \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨-3,1,-2⟩ & =-27\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $r=⟨-5-3t,t,1⟩$ into the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨-3,1,-2⟩ & =-27 \\\\ ⟨-5-3t,t,1⟩\\cdot ⟨-3,1,-2⟩ & =-27 \\\\ -3(-5-3t)+1\\cdot t-2\\cdot 1 & =-27 \\\\ 15+9t+t-2 & =-27 \\\\ 10t & =-40 \\\\ t & =-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to get the position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P,$ we substitute $t=-4$ into the equation of the line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =⟨-5-3(-4),-4,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨7,-4,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the intersection point is $P(7,-4,1).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-33203/ma-source-field/87c43102284dcfeb2638e146ab0d291e49c36333aab1eaa13bc29a1ec11c418e"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
